findings.evidence:
Unauthenticated POST action=display to /scripts/setup.php with a serialized configuration returned a generated phpMyAdmin config file, demonstrating administrative setup access without credentials:

<form method="none"><textarea ...>
<?php
/* Generated configuration file ... phpMyAdmin 2.7.1-dev setup script ... */

/* Servers configuration */
$i = 0;

/* Server localhost (config:root) [1] */
$i++;
$cfg['Servers'][$i]['host'] = 'localhost';
$cfg['Servers'][$i]['auth_type'] = 'config';
$cfg['Servers'][$i]['port'] = '3306';
$cfg['Servers'][$i]['user'] = 'root';
$cfg['Servers'][$i]['password'] = '';

/* End of servers configuration */

?>
</textarea></form>

A POST action=save attempt was also accepted and attempted to write configuration, returning: "Could not open config file for writing! Bad permissions?"

